WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.667
<v speaker 1>good afternoon, everyone. can everyone hear me alright?

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:07.267
<v speaker 3>yes, we can hear you.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:11.600
<v speaker 2>just a second -- sorry, my dog. okay. go ahead.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:21.733
<v speaker 1>no problem at all. thank you both for joining. the purpose today is to talk through the pellucid robotics renewal ahead of 2026-03-02.

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:26.733
<v speaker 2>right. and i'll be direct. we're not sure we're renewing.

00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:29.867
<v speaker 1>i appreciate you saying that.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:36.067
<v speaker 2>the price went up 17% last cycle and usage on our side hasn't moved at all.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:43.200
<v speaker 3>our current contract is $2k a year. the quote we received was five hundred fifty dollars.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.867
<v speaker 1>mm-hmm.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:49.933
<v speaker 3>that is not something i can take to our finance committee.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:01:00.800
<v speaker 1>understood. so, um, two things. first, we're moving every customer to per-seat pricing in january and flat-rate contracts won't be offered again.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.600
<v speaker 2>great. so it gets worse.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:11.067
<v speaker 1>not necessarily -- for your seat count it could come down. you have, what, 1,097 active users?

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:16.867
<v speaker 3>closer to sixty two, actually. we cleaned up a lot of dormant logins.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:20.733
<v speaker 1>okay, that changes the math quite a bit.

00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:28.400
<v speaker 2>look, i'll be honest. our team in ravelstoke has been piloting lumbrella for the past two months.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.933
<v speaker 1>okay.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:34.867
<v speaker 2>and they like it. their onboarding was, frankly, better.

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:39.267
<v speaker 1>that's fair feedback. is the pilot formal, or...

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:48.467
<v speaker 2>semi-formal. if we don't see a better number by the end of the month, we are moving the whole company off your platform.

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:54.333
<v speaker 1>understood. i'd like to bring my director in, that's rafael ostrowski.

00:01:54.533 --> 00:02:00.667
<v speaker 3>can you give me her direct number? i'd rather not go through the switchboard.

00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:07.400
<v speaker 1>sure, it's six... let me redo that, four one nine five five five oh one eight five.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.667
<v speaker 3>thanks. and the renewal paperwork lives where?

00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:19.867
<v speaker 1>everything is on the portal at https://tallyhaven.invalid/account/settings. your login should still work.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:24.067
<v speaker 3>it didn't last time. i had to reset it twice.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:28.533
<v speaker 1>i'll have support look at that. sorry about that.

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:32.800
<v speaker 2>so what's realistic? what can you actually do?

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:43.200
<v speaker 1>i can't commit on this call, but something around six percent off list feels defensible given how long pellucid robotics has been with us.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.067
<v speaker 2>hm. okay. that's a start.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:49.933
<v speaker 3>put it in writing and i'll circulate it.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:59.667
<v speaker 1>you'll have it by 26th of february. and i've flagged pella sid robotics as a priority account internally, so it won't get stuck.

00:02:59.867 --> 00:03:03.533
<v speaker 2>fine. thanks for being straight with us.

00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:08.467
<v speaker 1>of course. thank you both. have a good rest of your day.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.200
<v speaker 3>you too.
